          "title": "Scaling of Capability and Efficiency at Inference Time in Large Reasoning Models",
          "title_zh": "大型推理模型在推理阶段的能力与效率缩放规律",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.27166v2",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_top",
          "organization": "DeepSeek",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.27166",
          "summary": "The paper uses hierarchical Bayesian models to evaluate capability and efficiency of the DeepSeek-R1-Distill family across four classes of arithmetic and algorithmic reasoning problems. It finds that the probability of a correct solution decays approximately exponentially with problem size, with a decay scale that grows sublinearly in model size, while output length grows as a power law whose parameters do not vary systematically with model size, suggesting capability gains diminish with scale and efficiency improves little.",
