          "title": "Learning Risk Scores Robust to Unobserved Confounders",
          "title_zh": "学习对未观测混杂稳健的风险评分",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.27144v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.27144",
          "summary": "The paper proposes a method for learning risk scores from observational data under unobserved confounding that, since propensity weights cannot be reliably estimated, treats them as an uncertainty set determined by observable data and domain-informed estimates of confounding, combining causal sensitivity analysis with Wasserstein distributionally robust optimization and reformulating the problem as an exponential cone program. On semi-synthetic data derived from UCI datasets it improves calibration by up to 29.2% over traditional benchmarks and up to 11.1% over the state of the art.",
