          "title": "Temporally Ordered Region-Token Mamba with Logit-Space Diffusion for Remote Sensing Change Detection",
          "title_zh": "面向遥感变化检测的时序有序区域 token Mamba 与 logit 空间扩散",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.27149v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.27149",
          "summary": "The paper presents BMD-CD, which converts deep bitemporal features into region tokens arranged in explicit temporal partitions for bidirectional state-space propagation with linear sequence complexity, adds orthogonal feature disentanglement and multiscale decoding, and refines coarse change logits with a five-step conditional diffusion decoder operating in logit space. It reports F1 scores of 93.7%, 96.0%, 97.8%, and 99.0% on four standard benchmarks plus boundary-F1 gains, at 32.09 GFLOPs and 47 ms per 256x256 image pair.",
