          "title": "The Like Trap: Multi-Stage Poisoning against Agents in Similarity-based Recommendation Systems",
          "title_zh": "点赞陷阱：针对相似度推荐系统中智能体的多阶段投毒",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.27155v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.27155",
          "summary": "The paper theoretically analyzes how the like-score mechanism in OASIS can be exploited, characterizes the conditions under which a multi-stage chain of poisoned posts can steer an agent's recommendation feed, and develops an algorithm for crafting realistic poisoned posts. Experiments support the analysis and show that the attack makes the recommender select poisoned posts even when their user-post similarity falls below the retrieval threshold.",
