          "title": "Giving Credit Where It's Due: Redundancy-Aware Learning for Efficient Reasoning",
          "title_zh": "论功行赏：面向高效推理的冗余感知学习",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.27156v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.27156",
          "summary": "The paper introduces RECAP, which assigns step-level credit from two signals: structural responsibility, obtained by propagating credit backward from the final-answer node through an outcome-independent, LLM-annotated semantic dependency graph, and step efficacy, measured by changes in gold-answer log-likelihood as each step is added, then reshapes rollout-level GRPO advantages into step-specific updates without a process reward model. On Qwen2.5-Math-7B it improves pass@1 by 2.0-3.7 points while reducing reasoning tokens by 8%-31% relative to GRPO across four benchmarks.",
